sequenceDiagram
  %% env:sync on a container Instance: Orbit never renders an existing container .env again, so it writes only the attached connections' keys in place.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: env:sync
  %% kind: instance.connection_environment
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CLI->>GW: env:sync --instance=24
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit env:sync --instance=24`; Instance 24 runs in a container
  Note over GW: Admit the connection keys<br/>key names · paths · units
  %%> When:
  %%> - a running container, active, with no unfinished lifecycle work; hold its Instance lock
  %%> - key names of every attached connection and of the websocket app, each path's ACL egress rule, bridge endpoint and UFW rule, the private names, and the Instance's running units
  %%> - with no key to write, the run still starts: it withdraws a removed websocket app's path
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a stopped container or busy work start no run
  GW->>SW: Push lines to the vault<br/>env-5140
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the rendered lines hold the password; only the vault key name goes in the run input (R3)
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>connection-environment
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
  SW->>N: Write the connection keys<br/>Ansible · tags environment
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds the missing database egress rules, bridge endpoints and UFW rules; removes none of them
  %%> - reconciles the websocket path and a clone's own-site rules by description: keeps only the rules and the UFW rule the plan names, writes the plan's private names into `/etc/hosts`
  %%> - replaces each key's line in `.env`, adds a missing key at the end; a `${...}` value stays and is named
  %%> - every other byte stays; the lines reach the Node script on stdin, never argv or a log
  %%> - a changed file clears Laravel's config cache and try-restarts the Instance's running units
  alt keys written
    %% path: main
    N-->>SW: Key names per outcome<br/>written · added · kept · unchanged
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the written keys become Orbit-owned keys of Instance 24
  else file refused or phase failed
    %% path: failed
    N--xSW: env.configuration_invalid
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - a missing file, a link, or a quoted value that never closes leaves the file as it was; paths already added stay; a rerun is safe
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error code
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: Status and result
  end
